The 20% figure means raw-stock concentrate v/v, not neat odorants or w/w. Prepared stocks already contain DEP, DPG or TEC; do not remove or “correct” those carriers by subtracting guessed volumes from ethanol. Mixing contraction is unmeasured. Select a suitable vessel with headroom; do not assume an exactly brim-full 30 mL bottle is adequate.

## Before any physical transfer

- [ ] Match the physically labeled bottles to the now-resolved stock bindings and resolve the remaining exact-mass and safety holds; a printed schedule is not release authority.
- [ ] Match Orris **9% w/w DEP**, Alpha Irone **10% w/w DEP**, Ambrettolide **10% w/w DPG**, Tonkarome **20% w/w TEC**. Never use an old 30% Orris label as equivalent.
- [ ] Match the one user-confirmed AIMI / Methyl Ionone Pure bottle, the owned Indian vetiver and High Altitude lavender. No grade swaps.
- [ ] Cashmeran and Ethylene Brassylate are **neat/as supplied**. Do not use a desired-but-unprepared dilution.
- [ ] Confirm enough stock remains, each preparation is homogeneous, and the measuring equipment is appropriate. The smallest transfer is 20 µL (30 mL batch) or 10 µL (15 mL batch).
- [ ] Record delivered stock masses as well as raw volumes if exact supplied-product ppm w/w is required. No stock density is assumed from water or from the neat material.
- [ ] Use current supplier documentation and a competent formulation/safety review for intended handling/use. No flame or heat around ethanol; no skin test while safety is HOLD.

## Mass and carrier record

For measured stock mass m_i and product mass fraction f_i: product mass = f_i m_i; product ppm in concentrate = 1,000,000 f_i m_i / Σm_i. Known carrier mass for these single-carrier preparations is (1 − f_i)m_i. It is not automatically a carrier volume. For proprietary products/naturals, constituent ppm additionally requires a qualified composition.

Record for each row: bottle/lot identifier, preparation identifier, actual raw transfer, delivered mass, uncertainty, appearance and any loss. Keep DEP, DPG and TEC amounts separately. Compare sensory variants using a matched carrier matrix; V4-versus-V5 is a whole-formula comparison and cannot identify which change caused a preference.

Do not heat an unresolved solid to make a volume measurement or make an unstated dilution. If any bottle differs from this card, stop and rebase the formula before transfer.

